Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Reversible Timestamp Blurring for Spill Data", "Title"],

Cell["\<\
The dts1 transform: specification, reference implementation and verification\
\>", "Subtitle"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook document the process that is being used to \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]blur\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] the timestamp data that \
is generated by the darpa-spill-dump command.  The actual utility is part of \
the general DARPA-SpillServer package that is homed in the NOvADAQ git \
repository (but specifically Andrew\[CloseCurlyQuote]s modern git repo not \
the older one that we generated a long time ago from the SVN repo.

Things to be aware of:
This document as well as the mathematica library files (the .wl files) all \
live in the docs area of the repository.  You need both build_notebook.wl and \
dts1.wl to fully build this notebook.

I have an older version of mathematica so this is only tested on Mathematica \
12 but it should work on more modern versions.  The translation of this to \
the python code is portable to any modern python > 3.12

And this was originally put together in Oct 2026 so that give a feel for when \
it was last looked at.

\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0016716914342957`*^9, 
  4.001671984380703*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8313d6f1-11e7-4b11-91a2-\
5ee846192257"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Purpose/Problem", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0016719867383966`*^9, 
  4.001671988213051*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"36f31bd3-e632-4956-abb4-\
bd12fc0c76bd"],

Cell["\<\
The END (Experimental Neutrino Detector) needs timestamps from the NOvA \
timing system to trigger/constrain their detector data.  But for some unknown \
reason we were told that if the spill data was presented in its natural form \
and resolution then it could be considered CUI (I\[CloseCurlyQuote]ve had my \
CUI training and....no that is manifestly incorrect but we don\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t disobey orders)  The solution is apparently to degrade or \
obscure the true NuMI beam time.

So our solution is the following -- we are going to shift the actual beam \
spill time (based on the NOvAtime clock which is directly sync\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]d to GPS but runs at a 64MHz clock) by a small amount.  But \
we need to do so in a way that we can recover the actual time.  In this \
manner we can transfer and store beamtime data to external entities and then \
give them a procedure to decrypt/de-blur the times for real analysis.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0016719936708384`*^9, 
  4.0016723587203283`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b7c124ab-f4af-4bee-b099-\
5947a76a1de1"],

Cell["The Requirements I was  given/imposed were:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.00167236160732*^9, 
  4.001672386329074*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ac3791ff-2cf5-4312-97cc-\
7c02e04ce3f9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Assume a start from the output of ",
 StyleBox["darpa-spill-dump",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (CSV or JSON) ( this is the original source of truth)"
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001672394853463*^9, 
  4.001672422902392*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7b873913-2b64-4191-b553-\
ac538928bb4e"],

Cell["\<\
Shift each event's timestamp by a random offset in either a  positive or \
negative direction.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001672443420001*^9, 
  4.001672452178033*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7d23a30c-c762-437a-b2bf-\
69b03b3690ea"],

Cell["\<\
The actual distribution that the offsets are pulled from should be random \
variate  using either a flat distribution or Gaussian PDF (and really we \
could do any smooth PDF, but they wanted flat and Gauss) \
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001672457482101*^9, 
  4.001672561203578*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"934288d2-45a5-469b-a416-\
49eb8d5cfed9"],

Cell["\<\
The process should be fully reproducible.  So we are using deterministic \
tokens and seeds instead of something like a thermal rng or a time seeded on.\
\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0016725679568996`*^9, 
  4.001672665010508*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"949ade1a-da5c-467d-89d5-\
ae34a47957fc"],

Cell["\<\
The transform should be fully  invertible with only knowledge of the original \
token and the data value\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001672673415113*^9, 
  4.0016727107970657`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d2c4ed01-f7b6-4169-8d65-\
205e47fa4a24"],

Cell["\<\
The amount of blur should be tunable by the user but we also want to cap it \
so we don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t spin off into some infinity in the tails of a \
distribution.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0016727192720203`*^9, 
  4.0016727611083593`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"eb79882f-0311-40d2-bfdb-\
9e995b0428c6"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So this notebook defines the transform (version ",
 StyleBox["dts1",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "), gives a reference implementation, proves and tests its invertibility, \
characterises the variates, and examines what the blur does and does not \
hide. It is the specification the Python implementation (",
 StyleBox["darpa_spillserver.shift",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", command ",
 StyleBox["darpa-spill-shift",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ") is tested against."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001672769495825*^9, 
  4.001672773784449*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8d5c7186-a265-4808-97e9-\
0afaa89ebb67"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. Setup", "Section"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Get", "[", 
   RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"If", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ValueQ", "[", "$DTS1Dir", "]"}], ",", " ", "$DTS1Dir", ",", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"NotebookDirectory", "[", "]"}], ",", " ", 
           "\"\<shift\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      "\"\<dts1.wl\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$dataDir", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"If", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ValueQ", "[", "$DTS1Dir", "]"}], ",", " ", "$DTS1Dir", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"NotebookDirectory", "[", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<shift\>\""}], 
       "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7eb03d84-618f-4ce3-98f9-3eafaa193b4d"],

Cell["\<\
Define the nova clock frequency (64MHz) and maximum offset in nova clock ticks\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001672837174502*^9, 
  4.001672870078478*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ece7bdd9-d3c7-4e2d-af04-\
6d1f4266a54f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"$Ticks", ",", " ", "$MaxOffset"}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ad3eda7b-95af-451f-ad10-27f4db41052a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"64000000", ",", "32000000"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.001593408619813*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[3]=",ExpressionUUID->"ea44128e-3b58-4de0-9ca2-d5e2021c97ef"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One second is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["64000000", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e82f3305-b6f4-42c9-ae03-7099174dcdb4"],
 " ticks; the largest permitted bound, 500 ms, is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["32000000", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "40cad166-73e3-4bee-80c4-a42964ed7659"],
 " ticks.  When a shift is computed it is computed in an integer number of \
ticks so that everything remains on the same clock freq."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001672887059741*^9, 
  4.001672926751068*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3f20b8fa-0d52-453a-822d-\
d03be2a2f9be"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Input Data Format (and what to transform)", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0016729340780582`*^9, 
  4.001672947765704*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"fde56617-f6be-41fd-8d13-\
e6416680ae1a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The dump format of our input data has the timestamp in different \
representations (NOvA time, GPS time, UTC etc....)  Moving ",
 StyleBox["nova_time",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " alone would leave the true time readable from the others, so each must be \
considered.\n\nSo we read in a file and then split it up to work with it"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001672957778274*^9, 
  4.001673023508976*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"98893038-5989-45d3-940a-\
b82c82f3f4a1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sample", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Import", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
       "$dataDir", ",", " ", "\"\<sample_2026-10-12T0000_10min.csv\>\""}], 
       "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<CSV\>\""}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sample", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
    RowBox[{"sample", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"StringQ", "[", 
         RowBox[{"#", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "=!=", " ", "True"}], 
       " ", "||", " ", 
       RowBox[{"!", 
        RowBox[{"StringStartsQ", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"#", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<#\>\""}], "]"}]}]}],
       " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"header", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"First", "[", "sample", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"rows", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
      RowBox[{"header", " ", "->", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"Rest", "[", "sample", "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Length", "[", "rows", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"8a042547-8cf4-42f6-bcdd-faf212aafefb"],

Cell[BoxData["4701"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.001593408796968*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[8]=",ExpressionUUID->"18511d16-33f6-4258-967d-cee14441885a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Values", " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"rows", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{";;", " ", "6"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", "header"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b2884fc4-7953-482c-aa09-548facf6e407"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  TagBox[GridBox[{
     {
      TagBox["\<\"nova_time\"\>",
       HoldForm], 
      TagBox["\<\"spill_type_name\"\>",
       HoldForm], 
      TagBox["\<\"source\"\>",
       HoldForm], 
      TagBox["\<\"event_number\"\>",
       HoldForm], 
      TagBox["\<\"delta\"\>",
       HoldForm], 
      TagBox["\<\"pps_offset\"\>",
       HoldForm]},
     {"33885388992000001", "\<\"BNB\"\>", "\<\"tdu-near-master-ppc-02\"\>", 
      "178098", "64000000", "1"},
     {"33885388992000002", "\<\"BNB\"\>", "\<\"tdu-near-master-ppc-03\"\>", 
      "178094", "64000000", "2"},
     {"33885388992001413", "\<\"ACCEL_ONE_HZ_TCLK\"\>", \
"\<\"tdu-near-master-ppc-01\"\>", "1219019", "64001409", "1413"},
     {"33885389019521752", "\<\"BNB_TCLK\"\>", \
"\<\"tdu-near-master-ppc-01\"\>", "1219020", "27520339", "27521752"},
     {"33885389023789974", "\<\"BNB_TCLK\"\>", \
"\<\"tdu-near-master-ppc-01\"\>", "1219021", "4268222", "31789974"},
     {"33885389028058203", "\<\"BNB_TCLK\"\>", \
"\<\"tdu-near-master-ppc-01\"\>", "1219022", "4268229", "36058203"}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
    GridBoxDividers->{
     "Columns" -> {{False}}, "Rows" -> {False, True, {False}, False}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
         Offset[2.0999999999999996`]}, 
        Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
        Offset[0.2], {
         Offset[0.4]}, 
        Offset[0.2]}}],
   {None, OutputFormsDump`HeadedColumns}],
  Function[BoxForm`e$, 
   TableForm[
   BoxForm`e$, 
    TableHeadings -> {
     None, {"nova_time", "spill_type_name", "source", "event_number", "delta",
        "pps_offset"}}]]]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.001593408806018*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[9]//TableForm=",ExpressionUUID->"a4067a2b-235b-436f-b2b7-0066c22a84b5"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["utc",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["gps",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["unix_*",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " and the other time columns are functions of ",
 StyleBox["nova_time",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " and are simply recomputed from the shifted value. Two columns are not:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"946da418-cf0e-4f91-b4bf-ff7b0cb5bfd9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Counts", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<pps_offset\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Mod", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<nova_time\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "$Ticks"}], 
       "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "rows"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2fa54a27-db96-4317-a973-cfefdce47f45"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{"0", "\[Rule]", "4701"}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.001593408836281*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[10]=",ExpressionUUID->"1d6259ea-5fd3-438f-8cbc-377becc5ee69"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["pps_offset",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " is exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    TemplateBox[{"t","T"},
     "Mod"],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]]],
 " on every row: the sub-second phase of the true time. Left alone it would \
undo any blur below one second."
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"byKey", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Association", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<source\>\"", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<event_number\>\"", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "->", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<nova_time\>\"", "]"}]}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
     " ", "rows"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Counts", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"byKey", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<source\>\"", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<event_number\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
            "1"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"Which", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"MissingQ", "[", "p", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         "\"\<predecessor not in file\>\"", ",", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<delta\>\"", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<nova_time\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
           "p"}]}], ",", " ", "\"\<delta = t(n) - t(n-1)\>\"", ",", " ", 
         "True", ",", " ", "\"\<other\>\""}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",",
     " ", "rows"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c9b7d246-c042-4e20-802d-975944ebf8b9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"predecessor not in file\"\>", "\[Rule]", "612"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"delta = t(n) - t(n-1)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "4089"}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.001593408870648*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[12]=",ExpressionUUID->"0a001aa9-21df-49fe-b60f-1072c9149355"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["delta",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " is the gap to the previous hardware event on the same TDU, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["t", "n"], "-", 
     SubscriptBox["t", 
      RowBox[{"n", "-", "1"}]]}],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]]],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["n", TraditionalForm]]],
 " is ",
 StyleBox["event_number",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ". Chained from any one known time it would give back every other. On ",
 StyleBox["ppc-01",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " about 19% of predecessors are events the archive never stored, so ",
 StyleBox["delta",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " cannot simply be recomputed from neighbouring rows. (Over 1,052,663 rows \
on 12\[Dash]13 October 2026 the ",
 "same two relations hold without exception.)"
}], "Text"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. The idea", "Section"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\tEach time sample is tied to a specific TDU and has a specific event \
number tag.  The combination of the tdu source ID and the event number then \
gives a unique key for each event.  You can then define the transform  \
\[ScriptCapitalF](source, evt_no, crypt) and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalF]", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "23cf4cae-612f-4671-a90c-06ecad671fa1"],
 "(source, evt_no, crypt), the source and event number can be passed openly \
via the data file and then a single cryptographic key can be passed \
separately for the entire data set.\n\n Using this method we want only a \
simple shift then we note that \[ScriptCapitalF] = -",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalF]", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "9ae32d63-ae94-459a-891a-1b7bece237f3"],
 " which makes the forward and back transforms trivial.  To forward transform \
we just add the computed offset, to invert it we subtract the offset and \
nothing more than the event number, source and token are needed:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001673229038047*^9, 4.001673273276684*^9}, {
  4.001673330220252*^9, 4.001673434813019*^9}, {4.001673487228353*^9, 
  4.001673589093993*^9}, {4.001673620022805*^9, 4.001673729558919*^9}, {
  4.0016737639062443`*^9, 
  4.001673996849905*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b35189db-e4eb-4b94-89e1-\
16bcf8c7b68a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  TagBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["t", "n", "\[Prime]"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["t", "n"], "+", 
     SubscriptBox["o", "n"]}]}],
   HoldForm], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"aecfbaa8-\
3869-4754-b381-dcc7b3905bd6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  TagBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["t", "n"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox["t", "n", "\[Prime]"], "-", 
     SubscriptBox["o", "n"]}]}],
   HoldForm], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"db854cdd-\
f354-426c-9782-b5fcbab24590"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The other strength of this approach is that because there is no dependance \
or relation between ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["o", "n"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->"TraditionalForm",ExpressionUUID->
  "41e097a9-9f8d-4d91-8395-606a84e53d1b"],
 "and  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["o", 
    RowBox[{"n", "+", "1"}]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5e195d9a-d057-4cb9-968b-e7264d1f8a73"],
 " the process is well defined even if data is missing from the datafile or \
even if the file is scrambled.   This even applies to the time deltas between \
samples (since you can just add or sub the offset) :"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0016740090390673`*^9, 4.0016741495151987`*^9}, {
  4.00167419562379*^9, 
  4.0016742310011997`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b7ca98ba-58bb-4e1a-b110-\
09c600559ae6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  TagBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]", "n", "\[Prime]"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]", "n"], "+", 
     SubscriptBox["o", "n"], "-", 
     SubscriptBox["o", 
      RowBox[{"n", "-", "1"}]]}]}],
   HoldForm], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  TagBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["p", "n", "\[Prime]"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    TemplateBox[{RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox["p", "n"], "+", 
          SubscriptBox["o", "n"]}], ")"}],"T"},
     "Mod"]}],
   HoldForm], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each is a bijection with an explicit inverse, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]", "n"], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]", "n", "\[Prime]"], "-", 
      SubscriptBox["o", "n"], "+", 
      SubscriptBox["o", 
       RowBox[{"n", "-", "1"}]]}]}],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]]],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["p", "n"], "\[LongEqual]", 
     TemplateBox[{RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
           SubsuperscriptBox["p", "n", "\[Prime]"], "-", 
           SubscriptBox["o", "n"]}], ")"}],"T"},
      "Mod"]}],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]]],
 " (the latter because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"0", "\[LessEqual]", 
     SubscriptBox["p", "n"], "<", "T"}],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]]],
 "). When event ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"n", "-", "1"}], TraditionalForm]]],
 " is present, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalDelta]", "n", "\[Prime]"], "\[LongEqual]", 
     RowBox[{
      SubsuperscriptBox["t", "n", "\[Prime]"], "-", 
      SubsuperscriptBox["t", 
       RowBox[{"n", "-", "1"}], "\[Prime]"]}]}],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]]],
 " exactly, so the shifted file is self-consistent. None of this depends on \
how the TDU defines the columns: ",
 "the inverse is algebraic."
}], "Text"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5. Specification of dts1 algorithm and implementation", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001674249473569*^9, 4.0016742560938597`*^9}, 
   4.001674311879168*^9},ExpressionUUID->"afe9cbd4-4c4f-4d96-aa68-\
a37566340755"],

Cell["This is the description of the algorthim", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001674317556685*^9, 
  4.001674333734254*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"be258133-7b87-4858-a5cb-\
ef2ca4f3d8ad"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5.1 The Token", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001674339867208*^9, 
  4.00167434016006*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4997b662-58fb-4bcd-ba6d-\
b0f9c157b2b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The encryption token that we are going to use is actually going to carry \
more information in it then just a random seed value.  What we do is \
construct and pass a token that carries the random variate distribution, its \
actual parameters (in the NOvA time base ticks), and a 256-bit secret ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["K", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e7e446f7-ca23-4ae9-842c-82a4d658ebbb"],
 ".  So the form of the token looks like:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0016743500298643`*^9, 
  4.001674463944615*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f704ece7-e933-4962-910e-\
33231f2949d2"],

Cell["\<\
dts1:flat:a=A:<64 hex digits>
dts1:gauss:sigma=S:cut=C:<64 hex digits>\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"2ef389f1-fa70-4a7f-ad36-c83adf27ed9b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Where \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]flat\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] represents a flat \
box distribution and \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]gauss\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
represents a Gaussian with width sigma and maximum tail that is truncated by \
the cut.  The hex digits are the key value.  Holding the token is sufficient \
to both encode and invert. The part before the secret is the ",
 StyleBox["parameter string",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["P", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9a42cc05-c4eb-46f8-b52b-1564fa5e923c"],
 ", which is public and is mixed into every keyed block so that the same \
secret with different parameters gives unrelated offsets. And we constrain \
the parameters such that the width of the box A i ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"1", "\[LessEqual]", "A", "\[LessEqual]", "32000000"}],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "da00b369-f918-4f84-9c6a-d7f7100866d2"],
 "; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"S", "\[GreaterEqual]", "1"}],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c4470ff6-40a8-46f5-a0ef-cac2a9ff960d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox["S", "2"], "\[LessEqual]", "C", "\[LessEqual]", "32000000"}],
    
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d1b90496-7e62-4ea4-8eb3-f32b2af4dc1d"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001674467270516*^9, 
  4.0016746631802797`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ba8139a5-66dc-4465-9d15-\
be0b8c759aa7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["K", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e80c7909-c8d8-433b-b802-c6a381ef4fdf"],
 " is either 32 random bytes, or derived from a user seed with \
PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 (RFC 8018), with salt ",
 StyleBox["darpa-spill-shift/dts1",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", 600,000 iterations.  We aren\[CloseCurlyQuote]t overly worried about \
anyone wanting to \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]break\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] this, \
but a seed while convenient and reproducible is only as strong as the actual \
seed that is chosen (if you are using the SHA hash).  So basically if an \
attacker who can guess that you used your dog\[CloseCurlyQuote]s name....well \
they can invert the data."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0016747240784607`*^9, 4.001674765212297*^9}, {
  4.0016747993895082`*^9, 
  4.001674880265682*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7dd89fba-182f-40b4-846b-\
ca71dc68cd3d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The other thing to note is that a \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]public ",
 StyleBox["fingerprint\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ", the first 64 bits of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"HMAC", "(", 
     RowBox[{"K", ",", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<dts1 fingerprint|\>\"", "<>", "P"}]}], ")"}],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "04baf432-024e-41cd-9408-d3205ac01d8f"],
 ", is written into shifted files so that inversion with the wrong token \
screws this up and allows you to detect that you used the wrong decryption \
token rather than silently producing wrong times. And no it doesn\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t reveals anything about about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
   "the", " ", "real", " ", "K", " ", "that", " ", "was", " ", "used"}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"08aefec9-29f9-4d31-bc49-63b5fe0dd0b9"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001674916796726*^9, 
  4.001675017192812*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"268d521a-59d9-450a-a96c-\
9c1915f534eb"],

Cell["So mint some tokens:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001675070390958*^9, 
  4.001675077140411*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c66111da-10ae-4489-a54d-\
a73cafc7ceaf"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"tokF", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"makeToken", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"<|", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<dist\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<flat\>\""}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<a\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "3200000"}]}], "|>"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ByteArray", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Hash", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\"\<dts1 test vector\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<SHA256\>\"", ",", " ", 
        "\"\<ByteArray\>\""}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:=",ExpressionUUID->"03ea01f1-105e-44d1-9b10-29eb13c3623c"],

Cell[BoxData["\<\"dts1:flat:a=3200000:\
647f5c2495a4451550bd0faf3e4a0d7d8c5af77e26ec2a726a5a09660e7c78f2\"\>"], \
"Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.00159340890378*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[13]=",ExpressionUUID->"4239ee7c-0893-4bd3-8c60-ca8d7300bab9"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"tokG", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"makeToken", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"<|", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<dist\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<gauss\>\""}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<sigma\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "1280000"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<cut\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "3840000"}]}], "|>"}], ",", " ", 
    
    RowBox[{"ByteArray", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Hash", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\"\<dts1 test vector\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<SHA256\>\"", ",", " ", 
        "\"\<ByteArray\>\""}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ad047984-e029-45ff-b6d0-4709331fb6bf"],

Cell[BoxData["\<\"dts1:gauss:sigma=1280000:cut=3840000:\
647f5c2495a4451550bd0faf3e4a0d7d8c5af77e26ec2a726a5a09660e7c78f2\"\>"], \
"Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0015934089348516`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[14]=",ExpressionUUID->"bbe42759-c79e-4b7a-ac9f-77f78d0b613a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"fingerprint", "[", "tokF", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"fingerprint", "[", "tokG", "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:=",ExpressionUUID->"75eeca30-7f9c-4c0a-a372-75115de3106b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"7a63e2a2874c456f\"\>", ",", "\<\"42005a1faeae05cd\"\>"}], 
  "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.001593408946412*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[15]=",ExpressionUUID->"f4ba6912-d485-40c9-bf9a-291dc2518b51"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
These two tokens, flat \[PlusMinus]50 ms and Gaussian \[Sigma] = 20 ms cut at \
3\[Sigma] = 60 ms, are used throughout. Their secret is the SHA-256 of a \
public string: test tokens only.\
\>", "Text"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5.2 Keyed blocks", "Subsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For event ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["n", TraditionalForm]]],
 " of source ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["s", TraditionalForm]]],
 ", block ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["j", TraditionalForm]]],
 " is"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  TagBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["B", "j"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"HMAC", "(", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<SHA-256\>\"", ",", "K", ",", 
      RowBox[{
      "P", "<>", "\"\<|\>\"", "<>", "s", "<>", "\"\<|\>\"", "<>", "n", "<>", 
       "\"\<|\>\"", "<>", "j"}]}], ")"}]}],
   HoldForm], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["n", TraditionalForm]]],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["j", TraditionalForm]]],
 " as signed decimal integers. HMAC-SHA256 is a pseudorandom function: ",
 "without ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["K", TraditionalForm]]],
 " its outputs are indistinguishable from independent uniform bytes, and \
knowing any number of ",
 "offsets does not help predict another. Check against RFC 4231, test case \
2:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"StringJoin", "[", 
   RowBox[{"IntegerString", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
      RowBox[{"hmacSHA256", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"StringToByteArray", "[", "\"\<Jefe\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        "\"\<what do ya want for nothing?\>\""}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "16", 
     ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", "\n", " ", 
  "\"\<5bdcc146bf60754e6a042426089575c75a003f089d2739839dec58b964ec3843\>\""}]\
], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a1b7c90c-201d-48b3-8220-01e4926e7212"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.001593408976276*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[16]=",ExpressionUUID->"687a5ef0-1299-4454-986d-a4d9d32938c5"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5.3 Flat variate", "Subsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Read the first 16 bytes of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["B", "0"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " as a big-endian integer ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["X", TraditionalForm]]],
 " and take"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  TagBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["o", "n"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"X",RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "A"}], "+", "1"}], ")"}]},
      "Mod"], "-", "A"}]}],
   HoldForm], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is uniform on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "A"}], "+", "1"}],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]]],
 " integers ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "A"}], "\[LessEqual]", "o", "\[LessEqual]", "A"}],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]]],
 " up to a bias below ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "A"}], "+", "1"}], 
     SuperscriptBox["2", "128"]],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]]],
 ", about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1.9", "\[Times]", 
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"\[Minus]", "31"}]]}]]],
 " at the largest ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A", TraditionalForm]]],
 ". It uses integer arithmetic only, so every implementation on every \
platform ",
 "produces the identical offset."
}], "Text"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5.4 Gaussian variate", "Subsection"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Split each block into four 64-bit big-endian words ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["w", TraditionalForm]]],
 ". Each gives an exact dyadic uniform"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  TagBox[
   RowBox[{"u", "\[LongEqual]", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{FractionBox["w", 
         SuperscriptBox["2", "11"]]},
       "Floor"], "+", 
      FractionBox["1", "2"]}], 
     SuperscriptBox["2", "53"]]}],
   HoldForm], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "strictly inside (0, 1) and exactly representable as a double. The standard \
normal variate is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"x", "\[LongEqual]", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "AS241", 
      RowBox[{"-", 
       RowBox[{"1", "\[InvisibleApplication]", 
        RowBox[{"(", "u", ")"}]}]}]]}],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]]],
 ", Wichura's algorithm AS241 (PPND16, Applied Statistics 37, 1988), a \
rational approximation with relative ",
 "error near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["10", 
   RowBox[{"\[Minus]", "16"}]]]],
 ". Draws are taken in order, block ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["j", TraditionalForm]]],
 " = 0, 1, 2, \[Ellipsis], ",
 "word 0\[Dash]3, and the first with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{"x"},
       "Abs"], " ", "S"}], "\[LessEqual]", "C"}],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]]],
 " is used:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  TagBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["o", "n"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"Round", "[", 
     RowBox[{"x", " ", "S"}], "]"}]}],
   HoldForm], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Rejection gives the exact normal truncated to \[PlusMinus]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["C", TraditionalForm]]],
 " without needing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["erf", TraditionalForm]]],
 " anywhere. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["Round", TraditionalForm]]],
 " is to the nearest integer, ties to even. The constraint ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"C", "\[GreaterEqual]", 
     FractionBox["S", "2"]}],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]]],
 " keeps the acceptance probability above 38%, so the 256 draws available are \
never exhausted in practice ",
 "(failure probability below ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["10", 
   RowBox[{"\[Minus]", "53"}]]]],
 ")."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Exactness.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The specification is AS241 evaluated in exact real arithmetic ",
 "on the exact coefficients; this reference evaluates it at 60 digits. A \
double-precision evaluation agrees except ",
 "when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"x", " ", "S"}],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]]],
 " lies within about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["10", 
   RowBox[{"\[Minus]", "7"}]]]],
 " ticks of a rounding boundary or of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "C"}],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]]],
 "; there the Python implementation recomputes in ",
 StyleBox["decimal",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " at 50 digits. That makes the offset, and so the inversion, identical on \
every machine, which a plain ",
 "floating-point evaluation (whose ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["Log", TraditionalForm]]],
 " may differ by an ulp between C libraries) would not guarantee. ",
 "Section 8 constructs such near-tie cases deliberately."
}], "Text"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6. The flat variate", "Section"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"flat", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"offset", "[", 
      RowBox[{"tokF", ",", " ", "\"\<tdu-test\>\"", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], 
     ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "20000"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Min", "[", "flat", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Max", "[", "flat", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"N", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "flat", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"N", "[", 
    RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", "flat", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"N", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"2", "*", "3200000"}], " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "^", 
         "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "/", "12"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:=",ExpressionUUID->"79415083-a2d1-4df6-ac76-714892b503cc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", "3199164"}], ",", "3199992", ",", "1982.83075`", ",", 
   "1.849096681804632`*^6", ",", "1.8475211500819144`*^6"}], "}"}]], "Output",\

 CellChangeTimes->{4.001593429261346*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[18]=",ExpressionUUID->"c0574258-d660-435b-a969-c96704a4f8d7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Range, mean, standard deviation and the exact standard deviation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    SqrtBox[
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["1", "12"], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox[
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "A"}], "+", "1"}], ")"}], "2"], "-", "1"}], 
       ")"}]}]],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]]],
 " of the discrete uniform on \[PlusMinus]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["A", TraditionalForm]]],
 ". In milliseconds the bound is 50 ms and \[Sigma] = 28.9 ms."
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Histogram", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"flat", "/", "64000."}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "50"}], ",", " ", "50", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   "\"\<PDF\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<offset (ms)\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<density\>\""}], "}"}]}], 
   ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Flat, a = 50 ms: 20,000 events\>\""}], 
   ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "480"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"Red", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "50"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"1", "/", "100"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"50", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"1", "/", "100"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:=",ExpressionUUID->"988a618b-b16c-4d7f-a865-8d482007721b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[{
   {RGBColor[0.987148, 0.8073604000000001, 0.49470040000000004`], EdgeForm[{
    Opacity[0.33599999999999997`], Thickness[Small]}], {}, 
    {RGBColor[0.987148, 0.8073604000000001, 0.49470040000000004`], EdgeForm[{
     Opacity[0.33599999999999997`], Thickness[Small]}], 
     RectangleBox[{-50., 0}, {-48., 0.00975},
      RoundingRadius->0], RectangleBox[{-48., 0}, {-46., 0.009675},
      RoundingRadius->0], RectangleBox[{-46., 0}, {-44., 0.010675},
      RoundingRadius->0], RectangleBox[{-44., 0}, {-42., 0.0106},
      RoundingRadius->0], RectangleBox[{-42., 0}, {-40., 0.0098},
      RoundingRadius->0], RectangleBox[{-40., 0}, {-38., 0.010175},
      RoundingRadius->0], RectangleBox[{-38., 0}, {-36., 0.01005},
      RoundingRadius->0], RectangleBox[{-36., 0}, {-34., 0.00925},
      RoundingRadius->0], RectangleBox[{-34., 0}, {-32., 0.009475},
      RoundingRadius->0], RectangleBox[{-32., 0}, {-30., 0.010175},
      RoundingRadius->0], RectangleBox[{-30., 0}, {-28., 0.0102},
      RoundingRadius->0], RectangleBox[{-28., 0}, {-26., 0.0098},
      RoundingRadius->0], RectangleBox[{-26., 0}, {-24., 0.010175},
